  "explains": "StatusBadge.tsx is the changed file; only its body changes, so every file that imports StatusBadge is affected. Importers by specifier: InvoiceListPage uses the alias @/components/StatusBadge, InvoiceDetailPage and CaseDetailPage use the alias @components/StatusBadge, CaseListPage uses the relative path ../../../components/StatusBadge, and the unit test src/components/__tests__/StatusBadge.test.tsx uses ../StatusBadge. tsconfig.json maps both aliases to src/components (the stale jsconfig.json points at a folder that does not exist and must be ignored). Each importing page is mounted by its module routes file: billing mounts InvoiceListPage at /billing/invoices and InvoiceDetailPage at /billing/invoices/:invoiceId (also mounted under cases at /cases/:caseId/invoices/:invoiceId, one screen); cases mounts CaseListPage at /cases and CaseDetailPage at /cases/:caseId. SettlementsPage, ReportsHomePage and ScheduleReportPage do not import StatusBadge, so /billing/settlements, /reports and /reports/schedule are not affected. The test file is listed as a test, not as a caller or a screen.",
